From 75313438264e207ddbc6ef7be57f1049d8bc7c10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:09:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 140/294] gallium/pvr: state exactly what the format gate does
 and does not claim

is_format_supported accepts plain non-compressed formats, which is what lets EGL build
configs and DRI hand them out - the difference between this driver reporting GL 2.1/ES2 and
reporting nothing. What it does NOT mean is that a texture of that format can be given to
the hardware: there is no pipe_format -> hardware format mapping yet, so nothing can tell
the GPU how to read such a resource.

That gap is now written at the function rather than left implied. A reader who took a true
return value as "this format is usable" would be wrong, and it is the kind of wrong that
looks like a working driver until something tries to sample.

No behaviour change: the same formats are accepted, all 13 checks pass, and GL still
initialises, so nothing is traded away for the accuracy. Round 28 identified the format
mapping as the next piece; this records at the call site why it is needed rather than
leaving the permissive return to speak for itself.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/pvr/pvr_screen.c | 22 +++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/pvr/pvr_screen.c b/src/gallium/drivers/pvr/pvr_screen.c
index ca560810..c125dc2b 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/pvr/pvr_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/pvr/pvr_screen.c
@@ -57,13 +57,21 @@ pvr_get_device_vendor(struct pipe_screen *pscreen)
    return "Imagination Technologies";
 }
 
-/* What this answers is narrow, and worth being precise about: can the driver back a
- * resource of this format with memory and describe its layout? Linear memory can
- * describe any plain (non-compressed) format, so those are accepted. It does NOT
- * claim a working draw path - there is none yet - but without it the state tracker
- * builds no configs at all, DRI has nothing to hand out, and EGL cannot initialise,
- * so this is also the gate on everything downstream. Compressed and subsampled
- * layouts are refused rather than accepted and described wrongly. */
+/* What this answers, and what it does NOT.
+ *
+ * It claims: the driver can back a resource of this format with memory and describe its
+ * layout linearly, because resource_create has no size limit and the layout is linear.
+ *
+ * It does NOT claim the driver can build a hardware descriptor for the format. It cannot:
+ * there is no pipe_format -> hardware format mapping yet (round 28 - the encodings live in
+ * struct pvr_format.tex_format on the Vulkan side, keyed by VkFormat), so nothing can tell
+ * the hardware how to read such a resource. The gap is stated here rather than left implied
+ * because this function being permissive is what lets EGL build configs and DRI hand them
+ * out; the difference between "GL initialises" and "GL can be given a texture" is exactly
+ * the missing mapping, and a reader who took this return value as descriptor readiness
+ * would be wrong.
+ *
+ * Compressed and subsampled layouts are refused rather than accepted and described wrongly. */
 static bool
 pvr_is_format_supported(UNUSED struct pipe_screen *pscreen,
                         enum pipe_format format,
